Confirmed live: clock-skew-resistant JWT path produces 200 OK from GET /app, mints installation tokens cleanly, lists all 12 curiositech repos via installation auth. @octokit/auth-app sets iat=now exactly; on a laptop running 16s ahead of GitHub's clock that produces 'JSON web token could not be decoded' 401 (confusingly worded — they reject future-iat the same as malformed). Our getAppJwt now signs via crypto.createSign with iat=now-60, exp=now+480; getInstallationToken POSTs the JWT directly to /app/installations/<id>/access_tokens, bypassing the lib's internal signer. The createAppAuth path is left in place but unused by the patched routes.


